\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces  \textbf  {Regional organization of good-based and action-based choice signals.} \textbf  {(A--B) Representative choice-selective units.} Firing rates (mean $\pm $ SEM) are shown for a DLPFC unit selective for the left/right action (A) and an OFC unit selective for the earning/spending identity of the selected option (B), aligned to offer onset (left), resource-state update (middle) and choice switch (right). Trials are grouped by earning (red) versus spending (green) choice and leftward (solid) versus rightward (dashed) response; switch-aligned trials are grouped according to the choice made after the switch. \textbf  {(C) Population trajectories in good--action choice space.} TDR projected population activity onto an earning/spending choice axis (ChoiceES, horizontal) and a left/right choice axis (ChoiceLR, vertical). Columns show ACC, DLPFC and OFC. Red and green trajectories denote earning and spending choices, respectively; solid and dashed trajectories denote leftward and rightward responses. Large circles mark the population states at offer onset, and shaded regions show $\pm $SD across trial resamples. \textbf  {(D) Temporal encoding strength.} Encoding strength ($R^2$, squared Pearson correlation between population projection and the corresponding choice label) is shown for the left/right axis (blue) and earning/spending axis (olive) in ACC, DLPFC and OFC. Shading denotes $\pm $SD across 100 bootstrap iterations; the vertical dashed line marks offer onset.}}{10}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:choice_representation}{{6}{10}{\textbf {Regional organization of good-based and action-based choice signals.} \textbf {(A--B) Representative choice-selective units.} Firing rates (mean $\pm $ SEM) are shown for a DLPFC unit selective for the left/right action (A) and an OFC unit selective for the earning/spending identity of the selected option (B), aligned to offer onset (left), resource-state update (middle) and choice switch (right). Trials are grouped by earning (red) versus spending (green) choice and leftward (solid) versus rightward (dashed) response; switch-aligned trials are grouped according to the choice made after the switch. \textbf {(C) Population trajectories in good--action choice space.} TDR projected population activity onto an earning/spending choice axis (ChoiceES, horizontal) and a left/right choice axis (ChoiceLR, vertical). Columns show ACC, DLPFC and OFC. Red and green trajectories denote earning and spending choices, respectively; solid and dashed trajectories denote leftward and rightward responses. Large circles mark the population states at offer onset, and shaded regions show $\pm $SD across trial resamples. \textbf {(D) Temporal encoding strength.} Encoding strength ($R^2$, squared Pearson correlation between population projection and the corresponding choice label) is shown for the left/right axis (blue) and earning/spending axis (olive) in ACC, DLPFC and OFC. Shading denotes $\pm $SD across 100 bootstrap iterations; the vertical dashed line marks offer onset}{figure.6}{}}
